 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442982 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-2,1,4⟩+t⟨3,2,-6⟩,\\,Π:-4x+3y-z-11=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442982 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2968eff5-6f3b-5cf4-97d0-686663582eb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442982 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+3y-z-11 & =0 \\\\ -4x+3y-z & =11 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ -4(-2+3t)+3(1+2t)-(4-6t) & =11 \\\\ 8-12t+3+6t-4+6t & =11 \\\\ 7 & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442983 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442983 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108308" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442983 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442983 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-1,2,1⟩+t⟨3,0,2⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=13.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442983 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8e5d0c94-6cbf-5053-b8da-ce1333f1257b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442983 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =13 \\\\ ⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =13 \\\\ 1(-1+3t)-2+2(1+2t) & =13 \\\\ -1+3t-2+2+4t & =13 \\\\ 7t & =14 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-1+3(2),2,1+2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,2,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,2,5).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442984 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108315" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442984 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442984 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,-3,4⟩+t⟨4,-2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442984 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a985335b-cba4-5e25-b462-ecfeb2395155" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442984 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩ & =1 \\\\ ⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩ & =1 \\\\ -2(1+4t)+(-3)(-3-2t)+2\\cdot (4+t) & =1 \\\\ -2-8t+9+6t+8+2t & =1 \\\\ 15 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
